comment0.target=Canvas
comment0.text=\r\n Canvas is a class to allow for simple graphical drawing on a canvas.\r\n This is a modification of the general purpose Canvas, specially made for\r\n the BlueJ "shapes" example.\r\n\r\n @author\: Bruce Quig\r\n @author\: Michael Kolling (mik)\r\n\r\n @version\: 1.6 (shapes)\r\n
comment1.target=Canvas getCanvas()
comment1.text=\r\n Factory method to get the canvas singleton object.\r\n @return The singleton Canvas object.\r\n
comment10.params=area
comment10.target=void redrawArea(java.awt.Rectangle)
comment10.text=\r\n Redraws only the specified area of the canvas.\r\n @param area Area that needs to be updated.\r\n
comment2.params=title width height bgColour
comment2.target=Canvas(java.lang.String, int, int, java.awt.Color)
comment2.text=\r\n Create a Canvas.\r\n @param title title to appear in Canvas Frame\r\n @param width the desired width for the canvas\r\n @param height the desired height for the canvas\r\n @param bgColour the desired background colour of the canvas\r\n
comment3.params=visible
comment3.target=void setVisible(boolean)
comment3.text=\r\n Set the canvas visibility and bring the canvas to the front of the screen\r\n when made visible. This method can also be used to bring an already\r\n visible canvas to the front of other windows.\r\n @param visible boolean value representing the desired visibility of\r\n the canvas (true or false)\r\n
comment4.params=referenceObject color shape
comment4.target=void draw(java.lang.Object, java.lang.String, java.awt.Shape)
comment4.text=\r\n Draws a given shape onto the canvas.\r\n Only the affected area is redrawn.\r\n @param referenceObject an object to define identity for this shape\r\n @param color the color of the shape\r\n @param shape the shape object to be drawn on the canvas\r\n
comment5.params=referenceObject
comment5.target=void erase(java.lang.Object)
comment5.text=\r\n Erases a given shape from the screen.\r\n Only the affected area is redrawn.\r\n @param referenceObject the shape object to be erased\r\n
comment6.params=colorString
comment6.target=void setForegroundColor(java.lang.String)
comment6.text=\r\n Sets the foreground colour of the Canvas.\r\n @param colorString the new colour for the foreground of the Canvas\r\n
comment7.params=milliseconds
comment7.target=void wait(int)
comment7.text=\r\n Wait for a specified number of milliseconds before finishing.\r\n This provides an easy way to specify a small delay which can be\r\n used when producing animations.\r\n @param milliseconds the number of milliseconds to wait\r\n
comment8.target=void redraw()
comment8.text=\r\n Redraws all shapes currently on the Canvas.\r\n
comment9.target=void erase()
comment9.text=\r\n Erases the whole canvas without repainting.\r\n
